.TH LSB.HIST 5 "Volclava Version 2.2.1 - Oct 2026" "File Formats"
.SH NAME
lsb.hist \- bhist speed up configuration file
.SH DESCRIPTION
The lsb.hist file defines the parameters of bhist speed up. It is
.BR $LSF_ENVDIR/lsb.hist .
The installation creates a template in which the two required parameters are
left for the administrator to set; every other parameter is commented out with
its default, and the default applies until it is uncommented.
.PP
Each line sets one parameter as
.IR KEY = VALUE .
A misspelled or repeated parameter is an error: the loader and server do not
start, bhist runs standard bhist, and the message names the file and the
parameter.
.PP
Restart the loader and server after editing the file; bhist reads it again on
its next query.
.PP
The loader and server take their log directory and log level from
.B LSF_LOGDIR
and
.B LSF_LOG_MASK
in
.BR lsf.conf .
.SS Contents
.IP \(bu 2
LSB_BHIST_CONNECT_TIMEOUT
.PD 0
.IP \(bu 2
LSB_BHIST_DB_PATH (required)
.IP \(bu 2
LSB_BHIST_ENDPOINT (required)
.IP \(bu 2
LSB_BHIST_EVENT_DIR
.IP \(bu 2
LSB_BHIST_EVENT_POLL_INTERVAL
.IP \(bu 2
LSB_BHIST_HISTORY_RETENTION
.IP \(bu 2
LSB_BHIST_IMPORT_CACHE_SIZE
.IP \(bu 2
LSB_BHIST_JOBS_PER_BATCH
.IP \(bu 2
LSB_BHIST_MAX_CONCURRENT_QUERIES
.IP \(bu 2
LSB_BHIST_MAX_CONCURRENT_SCAN_QUERIES
.IP \(bu 2
LSB_BHIST_MAX_FORMATTERS_PER_QUERY
.IP \(bu 2
LSB_BHIST_MAX_QUEUED_QUERIES
.IP \(bu 2
LSB_BHIST_QUERY_DB_CACHE_SIZE
.IP \(bu 2
LSB_BHIST_QUERY_DB_MMAP_SIZE
.IP \(bu 2
LSB_BHIST_RECEIVE_TIMEOUT
.PD
.SH PARAMETERS
LSB_BHIST_ENDPOINT and LSB_BHIST_DB_PATH are required. The others are optional
and take their defaults when unset. The defaults suit most hosts; on a service
host with little memory or few CPUs, lower the cache and concurrency
parameters.
.SH LSB_BHIST_CONNECT_TIMEOUT
.SS Syntax
\fBLSB_BHIST_CONNECT_TIMEOUT=\fR\fIseconds\fR
.SS Description
Seconds bhist waits to connect to the service.
.SS Valid Values
1 to 3600
.SS Default
5
.SH LSB_BHIST_DB_PATH
.SS Syntax
\fBLSB_BHIST_DB_PATH=\fR\fIpath\fR
.SS Description
Absolute path of the database file. Keep it on a local disk of the service
host, not on NFS, which is slower.
.SS Valid Values
An absolute path
.SS Default
None; required.
.SH LSB_BHIST_ENDPOINT
.SS Syntax
\fBLSB_BHIST_ENDPOINT=\fR\fIhostname\fR\fB:\fR\fIport\fR
.SS Description
Host name and port of the service. The loader and server run on this host,
and management commands run only there; bhist connects to the server by this
host name. The server listens on this port on all IPv4 addresses of the host.
.PP
Use a host name, not an IP address.
.SS Valid Values
Port 1 to 65535
.SS Default
None; required.
.SH LSB_BHIST_EVENT_DIR
.SS Syntax
\fBLSB_BHIST_EVENT_DIR=\fR\fIdirectory\fR
.SS Description
Absolute path of the directory that holds
.B lsb.events
and its archives; the loader reads events from it. Usually leave it unset:
the loader then uses the cluster's own event directory,
.B $LSB_SHAREDIR/logdir
for Volclava or
.BI $LSB_SHAREDIR/ cluster_name /logdir
for LSF, whichever holds
.BR lsb.events .
Set it only if the event files are elsewhere.
.SS Valid Values
An absolute path
.SS Default
Determined from the cluster, as described above.
.SH LSB_BHIST_EVENT_POLL_INTERVAL
.SS Syntax
\fBLSB_BHIST_EVENT_POLL_INTERVAL=\fR\fIseconds\fR
.SS Description
How often the loader checks for new events, in seconds. A job change shows
up in bhist after about this long.
.SS Valid Values
1 to 3600
.SS Default
5
.SH LSB_BHIST_HISTORY_RETENTION
.SS Syntax
\fBLSB_BHIST_HISTORY_RETENTION=\fR\fIdays\fR
.SS Description
Days of job history bhist can show. More days need more disk space for the
database; make sure the disk holding LSB_BHIST_DB_PATH has room. Expired
history is removed after
.B lsb.events
switches files; jobs that have not finished may keep older records.
.PP
The database holds only events from files still in the event directory. If
the
.B lsb.events
archives are kept for less time, less history is available.
.SS Valid Values
1 to 365
.SS Default
30
.SH LSB_BHIST_IMPORT_CACHE_SIZE
.SS Syntax
\fBLSB_BHIST_IMPORT_CACHE_SIZE=\fR\fIMiB\fR
.SS Description
Database cache memory the loader may use, in MiB, both for the first import
and for reading new events afterwards. Lower it on a service host with little
memory.
.SS Valid Values
1 or greater
.SS Default
1024
.SH LSB_BHIST_JOBS_PER_BATCH
.SS Syntax
\fBLSB_BHIST_JOBS_PER_BATCH=\fR\fIinteger\fR
.SS Description
Jobs handled per batch by a large query, one that uses a time range or
searches all history. Lower it on a service host with little memory to reduce
the peak memory of large queries, at the cost of more batches and slightly
slower large queries.
.SS Valid Values
2000 to 50000
.SS Default
10000
.SS See Also
LSB_BHIST_MAX_FORMATTERS_PER_QUERY
.SH LSB_BHIST_MAX_CONCURRENT_QUERIES
.SS Syntax
\fBLSB_BHIST_MAX_CONCURRENT_QUERIES=\fR\fIinteger\fR
.SS Description
Queries the server runs at the same time; more wait in the queue. Raise it for
many users; lower it to reduce the load on the service host.
.SS Valid Values
1 to 128
.SS Default
16
.SS See Also
LSB_BHIST_MAX_CONCURRENT_SCAN_QUERIES, LSB_BHIST_MAX_QUEUED_QUERIES
.SH LSB_BHIST_MAX_CONCURRENT_SCAN_QUERIES
.SS Syntax
\fBLSB_BHIST_MAX_CONCURRENT_SCAN_QUERIES=\fR\fIinteger\fR
.SS Description
Of LSB_BHIST_MAX_CONCURRENT_QUERIES, how many may be large queries, which use
a time range
.RB ( \-S ,
.BR \-D ,
.BR \-C )
or search all history. Queries by job ID are not limited by this.
.SS Valid Values
1 to 16, and no more than LSB_BHIST_MAX_CONCURRENT_QUERIES
.SS Default
4
.SS See Also
LSB_BHIST_MAX_CONCURRENT_QUERIES
.SH LSB_BHIST_MAX_FORMATTERS_PER_QUERY
.SS Syntax
\fBLSB_BHIST_MAX_FORMATTERS_PER_QUERY=\fR\fIinteger\fR
.SS Description
bhist processes one query may run at the same time. A higher value can make a
single large query faster but uses more CPU.
.SS Valid Values
1 to 16
.SS Default
4
.SH LSB_BHIST_MAX_QUEUED_QUERIES
.SS Syntax
\fBLSB_BHIST_MAX_QUEUED_QUERIES=\fR\fIinteger\fR
.SS Description
Queries that may wait while the server is busy. When the queue is full, a new
query runs standard bhist instead. 0 disables the queue.
.SS Valid Values
0 to 4096
.SS Default
128
.SS See Also
LSB_BHIST_MAX_CONCURRENT_QUERIES
.SH LSB_BHIST_QUERY_DB_CACHE_SIZE
.SS Syntax
\fBLSB_BHIST_QUERY_DB_CACHE_SIZE=\fR\fIMiB\fR
.SS Description
Database cache memory one query may use, in MiB. It is a limit that is used
as needed; a large query may reach it. The memory is freed when the query
ends.
.SS Valid Values
1 or greater
.SS Default
256
.SS See Also
LSB_BHIST_QUERY_DB_MMAP_SIZE
.SH LSB_BHIST_QUERY_DB_MMAP_SIZE
.SS Syntax
\fBLSB_BHIST_QUERY_DB_MMAP_SIZE=\fR\fIMiB\fR
.SS Description
Part of the database file one query maps into memory, in MiB. This is mostly
virtual address space; the data actually read uses the system file cache,
shared by queries. 0 turns mapping off.
.SS Valid Values
0 or greater
.SS Default
256
.SS See Also
LSB_BHIST_QUERY_DB_CACHE_SIZE
.SH LSB_BHIST_RECEIVE_TIMEOUT
.SS Syntax
\fBLSB_BHIST_RECEIVE_TIMEOUT=\fR\fIseconds\fR
.SS Description
Seconds the server waits for a whole query request to arrive. Raise it on a
slow network.
.SS Valid Values
1 to 3600
.SS Default
5
.SH EXAMPLES
Only the required parameters, everything else at its default:
.PP
.RS
.nf
LSB_BHIST_ENDPOINT=hostA:3000
LSB_BHIST_DB_PATH=/var/lib/bhist-speedup/bhist-speedup.sqlite
.fi
.RE
.PP
A service host with little memory or few CPUs, with lower memory and
concurrency settings:
.PP
.RS
.nf
LSB_BHIST_ENDPOINT=hostA:3000
LSB_BHIST_DB_PATH=/var/lib/bhist-speedup/bhist-speedup.sqlite

LSB_BHIST_IMPORT_CACHE_SIZE=256          # loader cache 1024 -> 256 MiB
LSB_BHIST_MAX_CONCURRENT_QUERIES=8       # concurrent queries 16 -> 8
LSB_BHIST_MAX_CONCURRENT_SCAN_QUERIES=2  # large queries 4 -> 2
LSB_BHIST_QUERY_DB_CACHE_SIZE=64         # per-query cache 256 -> 64 MiB
LSB_BHIST_JOBS_PER_BATCH=5000            # jobs per batch 10000 -> 5000
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bhist-speedup (1),
.BR bhist (1),
.BR lsf.conf (5)
